description:
Found with emacs --batch on 29.3 (after patching the query error):
- function declarations get variable-name face (first declaration rule shadows the function rules);
- string interpolation/docstring faces never apply (whole-string rule lacks :override);
- _, •, _0 lex as identifiers, so the anaphor rule never matches outside strings;
- juxtaposed calls f[..] / g{..} (list_application / block_application) not highlighted; ⟦ x ⟧ contents get bracket face;
- prelude name list stale (~33 names missing; `assertions`, `iosm` don't resolve);
- imenu/defun names always 'Anonymous' (eucalypt-mode--defun-name asks for a declaration_head field the grammar lacks);
- indent-region is not idempotent: re-indents multi-line string contents (alters docstrings; 715/2431 lines of lib/prelude.eu change) and top-level ⟦{}⟧: declarations drift +2 each pass;
- quail rules translate ordinary code (in→∈, ni→∉, ((→⟨, [[→⟦, {}→∅, -o→⊝), docstring says |||| for |||;
- 28 byte-compile warnings (transient lambdas want #').

Observed driving `eu lsp` over stdio:
- never exits after shutdown + exit, even when stdin closes: main_loop borrows the connection so the writer thread never ends and io_threads.join() hangs (eglot hides it by force-killing);
- background type-check diagnostics are only drained when another client message arrives, so an idle buffer never receives them;
- a request with invalid params terminates the server instead of returning an error response;
- sends inlayHint/refresh and semanticTokens/refresh without checking the client advertises support.

Non-blocking findings from the rig-review of PR #1163 (eu-oaz72.65), comment https://github.com/curvelogic/eucalypt/pull/1163#issuecomment-6837417842:
(1) the doc comment of extract_declaration_name in rowan_ast.rs is now detached, above the new const;
(2) false positive: a checked non-test target nested inside a test- target is reported as never running;
(3) the HTML report still shows PASS for such a file; only the console and exit code fail;
(4) targets that rely on all-values-true, with no RESULT, are still skipped silently (documented limit);
(5) the docs say test-, but the code runs any name starting with test;
(6) has_checks is part of Target's Eq/Hash.
